
# Migrations are parsed byte-for-byte by discipline guards (vocab-drift/148, url-canon/150, authorityFloorFor/141)
# against LF-generating .mjs SoT. Force LF on checkout so a Windows autocrlf checkout does not false-fail the
# byte-identical guards (operator ruling 2026-07-04, guard-fix 2a).
fsi-app/supabase/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf

# ── EXTENDED 2026-08-12: the same rule, for every file a gate READS ──────────────────────────────────
#
# WHY. The 2026-07-04 ruling above fixed one instance of a CLASS. On 2026-08-12 the class reappeared
# somewhere else: with core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout gave F25's import-graph regex CRLF text, so
# the fitness runner reported 14-17 violations locally on a clean worktree while real GitHub Actions CI
# (Linux, LF) reported 0 on the byte-identical commit 3533e127. Someone had to reproduce it on a fresh
# origin/master worktree and cross-check the Actions log to prove the local red was fake.
#
# That is an hour spent proving a tool wrong, and it recurs for every new line-anchored predicate. The
# durable fix is checkout parity, not per-regex CRLF tolerance: patching regexes one at a time leaves the
# next predicate exposed and the next person to run the battery on Windows misled again.
#
# SCOPE: every extension the discipline layer reads (.discipline/ engine + fitness + governance +
# consistency all read source, config, docs and shell as text and match line-anchored patterns).
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`, so a future binary or Windows-native script is not
# silently rewritten; add extensions here as they are introduced.
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.cjs  text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf

# Belt and braces: these are read byte-for-byte by the codegen drift guards, so an editor that helpfully
# "fixes" line endings must not be able to make a generated file differ from its generator's output.
fsi-app/src/lib/contracts/**  text eol=lf
fsi-app/.discipline/**        text eol=lf

# NOTE FOR WINDOWS CHECKOUTS: this only takes effect on files as they are re-checked-out. After merging,
# run `git add --renormalize .` once (or delete and re-checkout the tree) so an existing CRLF working copy
# is converted; until then a stale local copy can still show the phantom failures described above.
